---
/**
 * A borderless pill holding one synthesised goal (1-2 lines), for the Goals
 * chapter. The Goals row is a CSS grid (see audit-logs.mdx), whose
 * `auto-fit`/`minmax(1fr)` columns stretch every chip to its column's full
 * width — no `max-width` here, unlike an earlier version, since capping a
 * chip's width left a gap between the last column of a full row and the
 * page edge instead of letting it fill the column like `StatTile` does.
 *
 * Grid also blockifies this element's `inline-flex`, which is why
 * `align-items: flex-start` still does its job: a grid/flex item's own
 * default cross-axis stretch would otherwise match every chip in a row to
 * the tallest one's height, and flex-start keeps a shorter chip's text
 * pinned to its own top edge instead of centering into that borrowed space.
 */
---

<span class="goal-chip type-body">
	<slot />
</span>

<style>
	.goal-chip {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: flex-start;
		border-radius: var(--radius-md);
		background: var(--bg-raised);
		color: var(--text);
		padding: var(--spacing-lg) var(--spacing-xl);
	}
</style>
